import tests/games/snake/rules.dl

set game to a new snake session
begin a run in the address of game
set game's food to a snake cell at 13 and 12
advance the snake in the address of game
print line game's score
print line game's length
print line (game's food is occupied in the address of game)
turn the address of game toward 3
print line game's direction
turn the address of game toward 0
turn the address of game toward 3
print line game's direction
advance the snake in the address of game
print line (the item at 0 in (game's body))'s row
pause or resume the address of game
set {paused steps} to game's steps
update the address of game after 0.25 seconds
print line (game's steps = paused steps)
pause or resume the address of game
set game's wrap edges to true
set game's direction to 1
store a snake cell at 23 and 0 into game's body at 0
advance the snake in the address of game
print line (the item at 0 in (game's body))'s column
set game's wrap edges to false
store a snake cell at 23 and 0 into game's body at 0
advance the snake in the address of game
print line (game's phase = the finished screen)
close the address of game

# Moving into the tail is legal when that cell is vacated on this turn.
set game to a new snake session
begin a run in the address of game
set game's length to 4
store a snake cell at 5 and 5 into game's body at 0
store a snake cell at 5 and 6 into game's body at 1
store a snake cell at 4 and 6 into game's body at 2
store a snake cell at 4 and 5 into game's body at 3
set game's direction to 3
set game's food to a snake cell at 20 and 20
advance the snake in the address of game
require condition (game's phase = the playing screen) reporting "The vacating tail blocked a legal turn"
require condition ((the item at 0 in (game's body)) is the same cell as (a snake cell at 4 and 5)) reporting "The snake did not enter the vacating tail cell"

# Entering any other occupied cell ends the run without changing the body.
store a snake cell at 5 and 5 into game's body at 0
store a snake cell at 5 and 6 into game's body at 1
set game's direction to 2
advance the snake in the address of game
require condition (game's phase = the finished screen) reporting "Self collision did not end the run"

# Simulation uses fixed steps, and a restart keeps the user's preferences and best.
begin a run in the address of game
update the address of game after 0.06 seconds
require condition (game's steps = 0) reporting "A partial step advanced the snake"
update the address of game after 0.06 seconds
require condition (game's steps = 1) reporting "Two partial steps did not make one full step"
set game's best score to 19
set game's pace to 2
set game's wrap edges to true
set game's show grid to false
set game's reduced motion to true
set game's palette to 2
begin a run in the address of game
require condition ((game's best score = 19) and (game's score = 0)) reporting "Restart did not preserve the best score and reset the current score"
require condition ((game's pace = 2) and game's wrap edges) reporting "Restart changed game preferences"
require condition ((game's show grid = false) and (game's reduced motion and (game's palette = 2))) reporting "Restart changed visual preferences"
require condition ((game's elapsed = 0.0) and ((game's steps = 0) and (game's length = 5))) reporting "Restart did not reset the simulation"

# The final free cell produces a win without trying to place more food.
set game's length to the snake board capacity - 1
set game's direction to 1
store a snake cell at 22 and 23 into game's body at 0
set index to 0
loop while index < the snake board capacity - 2:
    store a snake cell at (index mod the snake board width) and (index / the snake board width) into game's body at (index + 1)
    increment index
set game's food to a snake cell at 23 and 23
advance the snake in the address of game
require condition ((game's phase = the completed screen) and (game's length = the snake board capacity)) reporting "Filling the board did not complete the game"
close the address of game
print line "Snake rules passed"
